raising money from the BDC  I got a question from one of my YouTube  viewers one who wrote in to say I live  in Toronto I went to the BDC and that  stands for Business Development Bank of  Canada and you know they lend money to  startups they don't ask for collateral  and he wanted my advice on what to do do  I know about them should he work with  them or not this is more of interest to  my Canadian audience but there's  implications that will impact you if  you're trying to raise money from  anybody that I'll share in the video the  BDC is a crown corporation it started by  the government and they're really trying  to be a bank of last resort a lender of  last resort so they will touch the  businesses that banks don't want to  touch because it's too risky I've done a  lot of work with the BBC I didn't raise  money myself as an entrepreneur but when  I was in the venture capital business I  partnered up with them a lot the thing  with the BBC is they will usually two  things one ask for more so because  they're taking on a riskier project  they're going to take a higher interest  rate so if you can get a loan from a  bank or the BBC I'd go to the bank first  because you'll get a better rate but you  may not have an option and that's what  the BBC is there for if you can't get an  option then you go to the BTC and you  pay more the second thing with the BBC  is often they will want you to work with  their experts so part of the money will  go towards hiring a consultant to help  you with whatever problem you're facing  right now if it's branding or growth or  marketing or finance whatever it is  often they'll recommend that you use one  of their experts and they're their third  party to come in and help you and part  of the money that they'll give you is to  to hire that person so you have to be  okay with that you have to want to use  their expert and and like them and agree  with them and you know have a good  relationship with them so those are the  two things about the BBC I would  definitely explore the option but I  would back up before that and see do you  really need to raise money you know if  you're just starting out a bit  this I hate spending money until I'm  making money and I always try to find a  way to start small even start with the  service get close to your customers get  to know them prove that what you have in  mind will work start building something  up and then when you're ready to expand  if you show that you can get some people  to pay for this thing whatever your  product or service your salad you didn't  mention in your email prove that it  works go get some customers then when  you go talk to any kind of financial  institution you're raising marketing  capital you're raising expansion capital  it's a lot easier to get you'll get way  better rates you'll have people climbing  over themselves to work with you and you  won't have to give up as much of your  business so if the only person is  willing to touch you is the BDC right  now who's the lender of last resort and  there may be something wrong with your  business you may want to think about  starting up without going into debt  without taking on this startup capital  and building it up from there now if  they're not asking for collateral then  there's not as much of a downside right  if it fails they're not taking your  house but it's gonna be on your record  and the next time you go for capital  from any bank BDC angel investor whoever  it is they're gonna see that you took  out this money and you didn't make it  work so that's the risk you become  harder to work with in the future if  this venture doesn't work out so I'd  really focus in on trying to get money  start a service start small have a big  vision but start small get capital in  from your customers keep building it up  and when you're ready to expand when  you've shown that your proof of concept  works then it's going out talking to the  guys if it's bankers angel investors  venture capitalists to really build it  up but you may not even need to get  there there's nothing wrong with  bootstrapping a business and taking it  up so those are my thoughts on the BDC  great potential partner to work with but  I'd really start above that and really  look at you really need to go and get  financing or not believe those you're  watching like the video please give it a  thumbs up  and if you have a question about the BDC  about raising capital from banks about  raising capital for your business or any  other question for your company leave it  below in the comments  I love seem to come in and I love making  video responses for you thank you and  I'll see you soon
 

